Programme exports should survive odd cohort entries that LADOK will not
resolve as real student-course results.  We keep a local [[warn]] helper
that routes through this module's [[logger]] rather than importing
[[ladok3.cli.warn]], because [[ladok3.cli]] already imports
[[ladok3.data]] (to wire its subparser); the reverse import would
close that cycle.  Keeping the symbol as a function---instead of
inlining [[logger.warning(...)]] at every call site---also lets existing
tests continue to capture warnings with
[[monkeypatch.setattr(ladok3.data, "warn", warnings.append)]].
<<functions>>=
def warn(msg):
  """Log a warning message via this module's logger."""
  logger.warning(msg)
