\subsection{Setting up the [[course]] command options}

We add a subparser for [[ladok course]].
We set it up to use the function [[course_command]].
<<add data parser to parser>>=
data_parser = parser.add_parser("course",
  help="Returns course results data in CSV form",
  description="""
Returns the results in CSV form for all students on a course round.
By default, all students are included.
Use --exclude-reregistered to exclude students who reregistered.
Use --exclude-credit-transfers to exclude students with credit transfers.
""".strip())
data_parser.set_defaults(func=course_command)
@


\subsection{Setting up the [[program]] command options}

The [[program]] subcommand exports the course results for one or more cohorts.
The cohort is defined by a program code and, optionally, one or more program
round codes.
We set up that parser to use [[program_command]].
<<add program parser to parser>>=
program_parser = parser.add_parser("program",
  help="Returns program cohort results data in CSV form",
  description="""
Returns the results in CSV form for the students in one or more program rounds.
Each row describes a course result for a student in the cohort.
Use --round to restrict the export to particular program round codes.
""".strip())
program_parser.set_defaults(func=program_command)
@


\section{Producing course data}

We fetch the data from LADOK and print it in CSV format to standard out 
([[sys.stdout]]).
This way the user can deal with how to store the data.
<<produce data about course specified in args>>=
data_writer = csv.writer(sys.stdout, delimiter=args.delimiter)
course_rounds = filter_rounds(
                        ladok.search_course_rounds(code=args.course_code),
                        args.rounds)

if args.header:
  data_writer.writerow(course_header())
for course_round in course_rounds:
  data = extract_data_for_round(ladok, course_round, args)

  for student, component, grade, time in data:
    data_writer.writerow(course_row(course_round, student, component,
                                    grade, time))
@ We must take a course code and a delimiter as arguments.
We also want to know if we want a header or not.
