\section{Extracting data for a round}

Now we want to extract data for a given course round.
This is done by the function~[[extract_data_for_round]].
We need access to LADOK through the [[ladok]] object of type [[LadokSession]].
We also need the course round through the [[course_round]] object of type 
[[CourseRound]].
Programme exports meet a looser kind of input: a cohort can mention a course
entry that LADOK later refuses to resolve as a real student-course relation.
That should not abort the whole export, so we warn and skip that one course.
<<functions>>=
def extract_data_for_round(ladok, course_round, args):
  """Extract student result data for a specific course round.
  
  Processes a course round to extract student results data in CSV format,
  filtering by students and components as specified in args.
  
  Args:
      ladok (LadokSession): The LADOK session for data access.
      course_round: The course round object to extract data from.
      args: Command line arguments containing filter options.
  
  Returns:
      list: List of result data dictionaries for CSV output.
  """
  <<compute start and length of the course>>
  <<get the results for the course round>>

  students = filter_students(course_round.participants(),
                             args.students)

  for student in students:
    student_results = filter_student_results(student,
                                             results)

    <<determine if student should be included>>

    components = filter_components(course_round.components(),
                                   args.components)

    for component in components:
      if len(student_results) < 1:
        result_data = None
      else:
        result_data = filter_component_result(component,
                                student_results[0]["ResultatPaUtbildningar"])

      if not result_data:
        grade = "-"
        normalized_date = None
      else:
        <<extract grade and normalized date from result data>>

      <<yield [[student, component, grade]] and date>>

def extract_data_for_program_round(ladok, program_round, args):
  """Extract course result data for one program round.

  Enumerates the students in the selected cohort and then walks their course
  participations so completed courses remain part of the export.
  """
  students = filter_students(
    program_round_participants(ladok, program_round),
    args.students)

  for student in students:
    for course in filter_courses(program_round_courses(ladok, student),
                                 args.courses):
      try:
        results = course.results()
      except ladok3.LadokAPIError as err:
        warn(f"skipping course {course.code} ({course.round_code}) "
             f"for student {student.ladok_id}: {err}")
        continue

      if not should_include(ladok, student, course, results,
                            args.exclude_reregistered):
        continue

      for component, grade, time in extract_data_for_course_registration(
          course, args):
        yield course, student.ladok_id if args.ladok_id else student, \
          component, grade, time
@

The program exporter needs to recover real [[Student]] and
[[CourseRegistration]] objects from the lower-level JSON responses.
That keeps the rest of the export logic on the same abstractions as the rest of
the codebase.

We deliberately fetch the courses with
[[student_course_registrations_JSON]] --- the wide, all-history view ---
rather than [[student_course_participations_JSON]].  Results export must
see completed courses, and the latter method narrows to \emph{current}
participations for accounts holding programme-level Ladok roles.
<<functions>>=
def program_round_participants(ladok, program_round):
  """Return Student objects for a program round."""
  participants = ladok.program_round_participants_JSON(program_round["Uid"])
  return [ladok.get_student(participant["Student"]["Uid"])
          for participant in participants]

def program_round_courses(ladok, student):
  """Return all historical course registrations for a student."""
  courses = []
  for registration in ladok.student_course_registrations_JSON(student.ladok_id):
    try:
      course_data = registration["Utbildningsinformation"]
    except KeyError:
      continue
    courses.append(ladok3.CourseRegistration(
      ladok=ladok,
      student=student,
      **course_data))
  return courses

def filter_courses(all_courses, desired_courses):
  """Return only the course registrations with codes in desired_courses."""
  if not desired_courses:
    return all_courses
  return filter(
    lambda x: x.code in desired_courses,
    all_courses
  )

def extract_data_for_course_registration(course, args):
  """Extract result data for one student's course registration."""
  course_start = course.start
  course_length = course.end - course_start

  for component in filter_components(course.components(), args.components):
    result_data = filter_course_registration_result(course, component)
    if not result_data:
      grade = "-"
      normalized_date = None
    else:
      <<extract grade and normalized date from result data>>

    yield component, grade, \
      normalized_date if args.normalize_date \
                      else result_data["Examinationsdatum"] if result_data \
                                                            else None

def filter_course_registration_result(course, component):
  """Return result data for one component in a course registration."""
  component_results = ladok3.filter_on_keys(course.results(), component=component)
  if not component_results:
    return None

  result = component_results[0]
  if not result.grade or not result.date:
    return None
  return {
    "Betygsgradsobjekt": {"Kod": result.grade.code},
    "Examinationsdatum": result.date,
  }
@

